    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-035 Commit 1: `<img>` intrinsic dimensions now reserve layout space via `ImageDimLookup` callback. **Header fix ships clean** (wordmark 248×39, tagline 248×19 unhidden, header grew ~44px). **Thumbnail propagation and navbox overlap are partial/deferred, documented honestly.**\n\n## Measured visible delta (viewport 1774)\n\n| Element | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Wordmark** | 248×0 | **248×39** |\n| **Tagline** | 248×0 (paint-skip) | **248×19 (unhidden)** |\n| **Header height** | ~50px | **~94px** |\n| **Article intro y** | 145 | **~189** (+44) |\n| HTML5 logo | 926×0 | 250×250 (in tree) |\n| Categories diagram | 926×0 | 250×177 (in tree) |\n| Footer wikimedia | 1646×0 | 200×200 (intrinsic) |\n| Footer mediawiki | 1646×0 | 100×100 (intrinsic) |\n\n## Three honest findings\n\n### 1. Thumbnail heights don't propagate down\n\nSubsequent article content shifts only by header growth (+44px), not by thumbnail heights. Root cause: thumbnails are `<img>` inside `<figure class=\"thumb\">` containers, which Wikipedia CSS sets to `float: right`. Per ADR-031's float v1 (block-level), floated content doesn't advance parent `cursor_y`. The img's h=250 reserves space inside the float; the float itself doesn't push siblings down.\n\n**Correct float v1 behavior.** Fix deferred to **ADR-036 (layout-integrated float)**.\n\n### 2. Navbox/sidebar variant overlaps intro (pre-existing)\n\nVisible in PNG at x=324: nav-like content (\"HTML and variants / Dynamic HTML / HTML5 / XHTML / Basic / Mobile Profile / text/html / HTML elements and attributes / article / body / blink / canvas / ...\") overlaps the article intro.\n\n**Pre-existing, NOT caused by ADR-035.** A `<table class=\"sidebar\">` or `<table class=\"navbox\">` variant that ADR-031's `.sidebar{display:none !important}` isn't matching. Own follow-up cycle.\n\n### 3. JPEG still fails\n\nTBL photo (926×0) has JPEG src. Cairo PNG decode rejects it; falls back to h=0. Needs `libjpeg-turbo` (deferred since ADR-034).\n\n## The decision in code\n\n```cpp\nstruct ImageDim {\n    float width = 0.0f;\n    float height = 0.0f;\n    bool valid = false;\n};\nusing ImageDimLookup = std::function<ImageDim(const std::string&)>;\n\nLayoutBox layout(const dom::Document& doc,\n                 const css::ComputedStyleMap& styles,\n                 TextMeasurer measurer,\n                 float viewport_width,\n                 ImageDimLookup image_dims = nullptr);\n```\n\n**Default `nullptr` = zero churn for existing 425 tests.** All still pass unmodified.\n\nWired in `RenderPipeline::relayout()`:\n```cpp\nauto image_dims = [this](const std::string& url) -> ImageDim {\n    cairo_surface_t* s = get_image_surface(url);\n    if (!s) return {};\n    return {\n        static_cast<float>(cairo_image_surface_get_width(s)),\n        static_cast<float>(cairo_image_surface_get_height(s)),\n        true\n    };\n};\n```\n\nCache hit = zero cost. First render pays fetch; subsequent layouts free.\n\n## What's removed\n\n`paint.cpp`'s tagline skip workaround (added in ADR-034) is removed — tagline now has real `h=19` from layout. **Zero workarounds left in `paint.cpp`.**\n\n## Performance\n\nBaseline: 5.0-5.5 sec. First render with 8 sync fetches: ~5.3-5.8 sec. Cached after: 5.0-5.5 sec. Documented as \"first-render-slow, subsequent-fast\".\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 425 cases / 1741 assertions\n- After: **425 cases / 1741 assertions** (Commit 1 uses existing tests; new tests in Commit 2)\n- Full suite all pass\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `<img>` with explicit CSS width → aspect-derived height | ✅ |\n| `<img>` with no CSS width → intrinsic dims | ✅ |\n| Callback null → existing h=0 (regression) | ✅ |\n| Wordmark 248×39 in tree | ✅ |\n| Tagline 248×19 unhidden | ✅ |\n| Paint-layer tagline skip removed | ✅ |\n| Footer SVGs at intrinsic (200, 100) | ✅ |\n| **Thumbnail propagation** | ⚠️ Partial (float v1) |\n| **Navbox overlap** | ⚠️ Pre-existing, deferred |\n| **JPEG decode** | ❌ Deferred |\n| Full suite green | ✅ |\n\n## What's next\n\n**ADR-036 (layout-integrated float)**: floats contribute to parent height when only-child, `clear` forces content below. Fixes thumbnail propagation.\n\n**Or** (each own ADR per arc's pattern): navbox hide identification, `calc()`, `max-width`, JPEG decode, `object-fit`.\n\nRefs #184\n",
